From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:41:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the tasks card can start minimized, by setting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wave 2 of the Zeo next proposal (docs/ZEO-NEXT-PROPOSAL.md §5.10, ask
17). `agent.tasks_card.start_minimized` (default false, today's open
card) makes patch 0037's card start as its pill. The Minimize control
still toggles it for the rest of the session; the setting only picks
how it starts.

Of the three surfaces §5.10 named, this is the only one that needed a
setting. Measured on d2a4fb6 before writing any: generic tool calls
(reads, searches, fetches, MCP calls) already start collapsed —
`EntryViewState::is_tool_call_content_visible` shows content only once
the call is expanded or awaits an authorization; terminal and edit
cards, which do open by themselves, already have upstream's
`expand_terminal_card`/`expand_edit_card`. Subagent cards show their
preview only when expanded, except while a permission is pending, which
must stay visible. Adding settings for those would change nothing; they
are documented in Zeo's README instead.

The new field joins `TasksCardSettingsContent`, `default.json` and
`TasksCardSettings`; every literal of the latter (two non-test, five in
tests) gains `start_minimized: false`.

Tests: tasks_card/start_minimized_tests.rs — the card starts open by
default and minimized when the setting says so. Verified 2026-11-09 in
the prepared d2a4fb6 tree: cargo check --tests and cargo clippy --tests
clean on agent, agent_settings, agent_ui and settings_content, cargo fmt
--check clean; tasks_card tests 196 passed; settings, settings_content
and agent_settings tests pass.
